,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|fact_pursuit|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-fact_pursuit-4-v3].text,"이준호 씨, 박지연 씨의 범죄 행위와 별개로 본인이 먼저 숨긴 사정을 인정하십니까.","Mr. Lee, please separate what you saw, did, and assumed, and set out the chronology of the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation.",イ・ジュノさん、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、ご自身が見たこと、したこと、推測したことを分け、時系列で整理してください。,李俊浩先生，请分开您看到的、做过的、推定的内容，并按时间顺序整理隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|fact_pursuit|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-fact_pursuit-4-v4].behaviorHint,"표면 사실을 확인한다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 책임을 피하지 못하게 정리한다.","Confirm the surface facts; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; organize the point so responsibility cannot be avoided.",表面上の事実を確認する。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。責任を避けられないよう整理する。,确认表面事实。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。整理到无法逃避责任。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|fact_pursuit|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-fact_pursuit-4-v4].text,"두 분, 책임을 줄이려 순서를 섞지 말고 숨김, 출금, 해지, 손실을 각각 답해 주십시오.","Both of you, please separate what each of you saw, did, and assumed, and set out the chronology of the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、それぞれが見たこと、したこと、推測したことを分け、時系列で整理してください。,两位，请分开各自看到的、做过的、推定的内容，并按时间顺序整理隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|fact_pursuit|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-fact_pursuit-4-v5].behaviorHint,"표면 사실을 확인한다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 책임을 피하지 못하게 정리한다.","Confirm the surface facts; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; organize the point so responsibility cannot be avoided.",表面上の事実を確認する。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。責任を避けられないよう整理する。,确认表面事实。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。整理到无法逃避责任。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|fact_pursuit|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-fact_pursuit-4-v5].text,"두 분, 이 사건의 순서를 밝히지 않으면 어느 책임도 제대로 판단할 수 없습니다. 각자 먼저 한 일을 말씀해 주십시오.","Both of you, please separate what each of you saw, did, and assumed, and set out the chronology of the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、それぞれが見たこと、したこと、推測したことを分け、時系列で整理してください。,两位，请分开各自看到的、做过的、推定的内容，并按时间顺序整理隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|1].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-1-v1].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 기초 질문으로 출발한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; start with a basic question.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。基礎質問から始める。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。从基础问题开始。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|1].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-1-v1].text,"두 분, 각자 상대보다 먼저였다고 느낀 이유가 실제 날짜인지 감정의 기억인지 구분해 주십시오.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|1].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-1-v2].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 기초 질문으로 출발한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; start with a basic question.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。基礎質問から始める。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。从基础问题开始。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|1].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-1-v2].text,"박지연 씨, 이준호 씨가 먼저 숨겼다는 마음이 왜 본인의 돈 실행을 앞당겼습니까.","Ms. Park, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",パク・ジヨンさん、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、ご自身がなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,朴智妍女士，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请说明您为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|1].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-1-v3].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 기초 질문으로 출발한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; start with a basic question.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。基礎質問から始める。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。从基础问题开始。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|1].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-1-v3].text,"이준호 씨, 형 사정을 숨긴 것이 박지연 씨의 계좌 감시를 부른다고 생각하지 못하셨습니까.","Mr. Lee, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",イ・ジュノさん、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、ご自身がなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,李俊浩先生，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请说明您为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|1].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-1-v4].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 기초 질문으로 출발한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; start with a basic question.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。基礎質問から始める。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。从基础问题开始。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|1].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-1-v4].text,"두 분, 서로를 믿지 못하게 된 동기가 어느 시점부터 돈 문제로 옮겨갔는지 말씀해 주십시오.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|1].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-1-v5].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 기초 질문으로 출발한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; start with a basic question.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。基礎質問から始める。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。从基础问题开始。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|1].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-1-v5].text,"두 분, 먼저 상처받았다는 감정과 먼저 실행한 행동을 왜 서로 섞어 말하게 됐습니까.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|2].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-2-v1].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 증거와 진술의 빈틈을 맞춘다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; line up the gaps between evidence and statements.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。証拠と陳述の隙間を照合する。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。对齐证据与陈述之间的空隙。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|2].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-2-v1].text,"박지연 씨, 먼저 배신당했다는 감정이 왜 먼저 돈을 빼야 한다는 판단으로 이어졌습니까.","Ms. Park, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",パク・ジヨンさん、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、ご自身がなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,朴智妍女士，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请说明您为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|2].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-2-v2].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 증거와 진술의 빈틈을 맞춘다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; line up the gaps between evidence and statements.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。証拠と陳述の隙間を照合する。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。对齐证据与陈述之间的空隙。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|2].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-2-v2].text,"이준호 씨, 가족 안의 갈등이 두려웠다는 이유로 돈의 흐름까지 숨긴 마음을 어떻게 설명하시겠습니까.","Mr. Lee, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",イ・ジュノさん、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、ご自身がなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,李俊浩先生，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请说明您为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|2].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-2-v3].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 증거와 진술의 빈틈을 맞춘다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; line up the gaps between evidence and statements.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。証拠と陳述の隙間を照合する。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。对齐证据与陈述之间的空隙。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|2].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-2-v3].text,"두 분, 각자 자기 행동을 방어하려고 순서 중 유리한 부분만 붙잡고 있지는 않습니까.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|2].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-2-v4].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 증거와 진술의 빈틈을 맞춘다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; line up the gaps between evidence and statements.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。証拠と陳述の隙間を照合する。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。对齐证据与陈述之间的空隙。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|2].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-2-v4].text,"두 분, 상대의 침묵이 내 실행을 정당화한다는 생각이 어디서 생겼는지 말씀해 주십시오.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|2].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-2-v5].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 증거와 진술의 빈틈을 맞춘다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; line up the gaps between evidence and statements.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。証拠と陳述の隙間を照合する。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。对齐证据与陈述之间的空隙。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|2].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-2-v5].text,"두 분, 이 사건에서 두려움이 책임 회피로 바뀐 지점을 각자 밝혀 주십시오.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|3].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-3-v1].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 숨긴 맥락을 드러내게 한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; draw out the concealed context.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。隠した文脈を明らかにさせる。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。引出被隐瞒的背景。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|3].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-3-v1].text,"박지연 씨, 이준호 씨가 먼저 숨긴 사실을 해지 서류 절차 문제의 이유로 삼은 마음을 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Park, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",パク・ジヨンさん、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、ご自身がなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,朴智妍女士，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请说明您为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|3].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-3-v2].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 숨긴 맥락을 드러내게 한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; draw out the concealed context.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。隠した文脈を明らかにさせる。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。引出被隐瞒的背景。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|3].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-3-v2].text,"이준호 씨, 형을 지키려는 마음이 부부 재산 신뢰를 깨뜨릴 수 있다는 점을 왜 외면하셨습니까.","Mr. Lee, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",イ・ジュノさん、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、ご自身がなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,李俊浩先生，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请说明您为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|3].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-3-v3].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 숨긴 맥락을 드러내게 한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; draw out the concealed context.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。隠した文脈を明らかにさせる。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。引出被隐瞒的背景。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|3].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-3-v3].text,"두 분, 돈이 사라진 뒤에도 각자 상대의 잘못을 먼저 말하게 된 이유가 무엇입니까.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|3].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-3-v4].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 숨긴 맥락을 드러내게 한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; draw out the concealed context.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。隠した文脈を明らかにさせる。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。引出被隐瞒的背景。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|3].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-3-v4].text,"두 분, 숨김의 시작과 범죄 행위의 무게를 왜 같은 저울에 올리려 했는지 답해 주십시오.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|3].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-3-v5].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 숨긴 맥락을 드러내게 한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; draw out the concealed context.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。隠した文脈を明らかにさせる。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。引出被隐瞒的背景。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|3].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-3-v5].text,"두 분, 결국 내가 먼저 피해자였다는 마음이 어떤 책임을 가리고 있었는지 말씀해 주십시오.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-4-v1].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 책임을 피하지 못하게 정리한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; organize the point so responsibility cannot be avoided.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。責任を避けられないよう整理する。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。整理到无法逃避责任。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-4-v1].text,"박지연 씨, 먼저 상처받았다는 마음이 왜 서류를 조작해도 된다는 결론으로 이어졌습니까.","Ms. Park, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",パク・ジヨンさん、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、ご自身がなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,朴智妍女士，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请说明您为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-4-v2].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 책임을 피하지 못하게 정리한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; organize the point so responsibility cannot be avoided.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。責任を避けられないよう整理する。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。整理到无法逃避责任。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-4-v2].text,"이준호 씨, 그곳에 갔다는 설명이라고 해도 배우자를 계속 배제한 책임을 어디까지 인정하십니까.","Mr. Lee, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",イ・ジュノさん、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、ご自身がなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,李俊浩先生，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请说明您为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-4-v3].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 책임을 피하지 못하게 정리한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; organize the point so responsibility cannot be avoided.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。責任を避けられないよう整理する。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。整理到无法逃避责任。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-4-v3].text,"두 분, 각자 먼저 한 잘못을 상대의 더 큰 잘못 뒤에 숨기려 한 것은 아닙니까.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-4-v4].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 책임을 피하지 못하게 정리한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; organize the point so responsibility cannot be avoided.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。責任を避けられないよう整理する。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。整理到无法逃避责任。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-4-v4].text,"두 분, 선후를 밝히는 일이 왜 두 분 모두에게 불편한지 그 이유를 직접 말씀해 주십시오.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-4-v5].behaviorHint,"행동 뒤의 판단과 두려움을 묻는다. 숨김, 감시, 실행, 조작을 분리해 시간순을 고정한다. 책임을 피하지 못하게 정리한다.","Ask about the judgment and fear behind the action; separate concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, then fix the chronology; organize the point so responsibility cannot be avoided.",行動の背後にある判断と恐れを問う。隠蔽、監視、実行、操作を切り分け、時系列を固定する。責任を避けられないよう整理する。,询问行动背后的判断与恐惧。分开隐瞒、监视、执行、操纵，并固定时间顺序。整理到无法逃避责任。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_question].entries[h-d4|motive_search|4].variants[judgeq-h-d4-motive_search-4-v5].text,"두 분, 이 사건에서 동기보다 무거운 것은 실제 행동입니다. 각자 그 행동을 왜 했는지 답하십시오.","Both of you, in relation to the order of concealment, monitoring, execution, and manipulation, please each explain why you acted as you did, without folding it into the other party’s fault.",お二人とも、隠蔽・監視・実行・操作の順序について、相手の過ちにまとめず、それぞれがなぜその行動を取ったのか説明してください。,两位，围绕隐瞒、监视、执行与操纵的顺序，请各自说明为什么那样行动，不要把它并入对方的过错。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|hard].variants[judgewit-w-1-hard-v1].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|hard].variants[judgewit-w-1-hard-v1].text,오피스텔 경비님을 즉시 모시겠습니다. 그 출입을 더 이상 정황 해석으로만 처리할 수 없습니다.,I will call the Officetel Security Guard at once. These entries can no longer be treated as mere circumstantial interpretation.,オフィステル警備員を直ちにお呼びします。その出入りを、これ以上状況の解釈だけで扱うことはできません。,立即传唤韩式商住公寓保安。那些出入不能再只按情况解读来处理。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|hard].variants[judgewit-w-1-hard-v2].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|hard].variants[judgewit-w-1-hard-v2].text,"오피스텔 경비님, 들어오십시오. 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황을 바로 확인하겠습니다.","Officetel Security Guard, please come in. We will immediately confirm the vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.",オフィステル警備員、入ってください。車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況をすぐ確認します。,韩式商住公寓保安，请进。现在确认车辆出入频率和该楼层的居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|hard].variants[judgewit-w-1-hard-v3].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|hard].variants[judgewit-w-1-hard-v3].text,오피스텔 경비님의 증언으로 동선을 확정하겠습니다. 외도인지 다른 사정인지 현장부터 가리겠습니다.,The Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will settle the route. We will start from the scene to determine whether this was an affair or something else.,オフィステル警備員の証言で動線を確定します。不倫なのか別の事情なのか、現場から見極めます。,将通过韩式商住公寓保安的证言确认动线。先从现场判断这是出轨还是另有情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|hard].variants[judgewit-w-1-hard-v4].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|hard].variants[judgewit-w-1-hard-v4].text,오피스텔 경비님을 부르겠습니다. 이 방문 기록을 더 미루면 쟁점이 흐려집니다.,"I will call the Officetel Security Guard. If we put off these visit records any longer, the issue will blur.",オフィステル警備員をお呼びします。この訪問記録をこれ以上先送りすると、争点がぼやけます。,传唤韩式商住公寓保安。再拖延这些探访记录，争议点就会模糊。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|hard].variants[judgewit-w-1-hard-v5].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|hard].variants[judgewit-w-1-hard-v5].text,오피스텔 경비님 증언을 듣겠습니다. 누가 그 층에 있었는지 지금 확인해야 합니다.,We will hear from the Officetel Security Guard. We must now confirm who was on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言を聞きます。その階に誰がいたのか、今確認しなければなりません。,听取韩式商住公寓保安的证言。现在必须确认那一层都有谁。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|mid].variants[judgewit-w-1-mid-v1].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|mid].variants[judgewit-w-1-mid-v1].text,오피스텔 경비님 증언이 필요합니다. 두 분의 해석이 갈리는 만큼 출입 빈도와 해당 층 상황을 직접 확인하겠습니다.,"We need testimony from the Officetel Security Guard. Since your interpretations diverge, I will verify the entry frequency and the situation on that floor directly.",オフィステル警備員の証言が必要です。お二人の解釈が分かれている以上、出入りの頻度とその階の状況を直接確認します。,需要韩式商住公寓保安的证言。既然两位解读不同，我将直接确认出入频率和该楼层情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|mid].variants[judgewit-w-1-mid-v2].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|mid].variants[judgewit-w-1-mid-v2].text,"오피스텔 경비님을 모시겠습니다. 오피스텔 방문을 외도 정황으로 볼지 다른 사정으로 볼지, 현장 기억을 들어야 합니다.","I will call the Officetel Security Guard. To decide whether the officetel visits point to an affair or another circumstance, we need to hear the on-site memory.",オフィステル警備員をお呼びします。オフィステル訪問を不倫の状況と見るのか別の事情と見るのか、現場の記憶を聞く必要があります。,传唤韩式商住公寓保安。要判断韩式商住公寓探访是出轨情况还是另有原因，必须听取现场记忆。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|mid].variants[judgewit-w-1-mid-v3].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|mid].variants[judgewit-w-1-mid-v3].text,정황만으로 판단하지 않겠습니다. 오피스텔 경비님께 차량 출입과 거주 현황을 바로 확인하겠습니다.,I will not judge on circumstances alone. I will ask the Officetel Security Guard to confirm the vehicle entries and occupancy status now.,状況だけで判断しません。オフィステル警備員に、車両の出入りと居住状況をすぐ確認します。,不会仅凭情况判断。我会立即向韩式商住公寓保安确认车辆出入和居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|mid].variants[judgewit-w-1-mid-v4].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|mid].variants[judgewit-w-1-mid-v4].text,"오피스텔 경비님, 방문 차량을 본 기억과 그 층의 거주자를 구분해서 말씀해 주셔야 합니다.","Officetel Security Guard, please separate what you remember seeing about the visiting vehicle from who lived on that floor.",オフィステル警備員、訪問車両を見た記憶と、その階の居住者を分けて述べてください。,韩式商住公寓保安，请把看见来访车辆的记忆和该楼层住户分开说明。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|mid].variants[judgewit-w-1-mid-v5].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|mid].variants[judgewit-w-1-mid-v5].text,오피스텔 경비님을 통해 같은 장소가 반복된 이유를 좁히겠습니다. 더는 추측만으로 둘 수 없습니다.,"Through the Officetel Security Guard, I will narrow down why the same place kept recurring. This cannot remain guesswork.",オフィステル警備員を通じて、同じ場所が繰り返された理由を絞ります。これ以上、推測だけにはしておけません。,通过韩式商住公寓保安缩小同一地点反复出现的理由。不能再只停留在猜测。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|soft].variants[judgewit-w-1-soft-v1].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|soft].variants[judgewit-w-1-soft-v1].text,"오피스텔 경비님을 모시겠습니다. 차량 출입이 언제, 얼마나 반복됐는지부터 차분히 확인하겠습니다.",I will call the Officetel Security Guard. We will calmly begin by confirming when and how often the vehicle entered.,オフィステル警備員をお呼びします。車両の出入りがいつ、どれほど繰り返されたのかから落ち着いて確認します。,传唤韩式商住公寓保安。先冷静确认车辆是在何时、以何种频率反复出入。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|soft].variants[judgewit-w-1-soft-v2].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|soft].variants[judgewit-w-1-soft-v2].text,오피스텔 경비님께 먼저 묻겠습니다. 해당 층의 거주 현황과 방문 빈도를 기록과 기억으로 맞춰 보겠습니다.,I will first ask the Officetel Security Guard. We will match the occupancy of that floor and the visit frequency against the records and memory.,まずオフィステル警備員に尋ねます。その階の居住状況と訪問頻度を、記録と記憶で照合します。,先询问韩式商住公寓保安。将用记录和记忆核对该楼层居住情况与探访频率。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|soft].variants[judgewit-w-1-soft-v3].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|soft].variants[judgewit-w-1-soft-v3].text,오피스텔 경비님을 부르겠습니다. 정황 해석보다 실제 출입 장면을 먼저 확인하겠습니다.,I will call the Officetel Security Guard. We will confirm the actual entry scenes before interpreting the circumstances.,オフィステル警備員をお呼びします。状況の解釈より先に、実際の出入りの場面を確認します。,传唤韩式商住公寓保安。先确认实际出入场景，再进行情况解读。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|soft].variants[judgewit-w-1-soft-v4].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|soft].variants[judgewit-w-1-soft-v4].text,"오피스텔 경비님, 들어와 주십시오. 이준호 씨 차량을 본 시간대와 횟수를 순서대로 듣겠습니다.","Officetel Security Guard, please come in. We will hear, in order, when and how often you saw Mr. Lee Jun-ho’s vehicle.",オフィステル警備員、入ってください。イ・ジュノさんの車を見た時間帯と回数を順に伺います。,韩式商住公寓保安，请进。请按顺序说明看到李俊浩先生车辆的时间段和次数。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|soft].variants[judgewit-w-1-soft-v5].behaviorHint,오피스텔 경비 증언이 차량 출입 빈도와 해당 층 거주 현황에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Officetel Security Guard’s testimony will bear on vehicle entry frequency and who lived on that floor.,オフィステル警備員の証言が、車両の出入りの頻度とその階の居住状況にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明韩式商住公寓保安的证言将如何影响车辆出入频率和该楼层居住情况。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-1|soft].variants[judgewit-w-1-soft-v5].text,"오피스텔 경비님의 기억을 통해 그 층에 누가 살았는지, 방문이 어떤 패턴이었는지 확인하겠습니다.",We will use the Officetel Security Guard’s memory to confirm who lived on that floor and what pattern the visits followed.,オフィステル警備員の記憶を通じて、その階に誰が住んでいたのか、訪問がどのようなパターンだったのかを確認します。,通过韩式商住公寓保安的记忆，确认那一层住着谁，以及探访呈现什么模式。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|hard].variants[judgewit-w-2-hard-v1].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|hard].variants[judgewit-w-2-hard-v1].text,은행 직원님을 즉시 모시겠습니다. 해지 서류와 해지 절차를 더 이상 모호하게 둘 수 없습니다.,I will call the Bank Clerk at once. The cancellation documents and procedure can no longer be left unclear.,銀行職員を直ちにお呼びします。解約書類と解約手続きを、これ以上曖昧なままにはできません。,立即传唤银行职员。解约文件和解约程序不能再含糊下去。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|hard].variants[judgewit-w-2-hard-v2].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|hard].variants[judgewit-w-2-hard-v2].text,"은행 직원님, 들어오십시오. 공동 적금 해지 과정에서 어떤 확인이 빠졌는지 바로 답해 주셔야 합니다.","Bank Clerk, please come in. You must answer at once what verification was missing during the joint savings cancellation.",銀行職員、入ってください。共同積立預金の解約過程でどの確認が抜けたのか、すぐ答えていただきます。,银行职员，请进。请立即回答共同储蓄账户解约过程中缺少了哪些核验。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|hard].variants[judgewit-w-2-hard-v3].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|hard].variants[judgewit-w-2-hard-v3].text,은행 직원님의 증언으로 서류 처리 과정을 확정하겠습니다. 해지 서류 진위를 지금 확인해야 합니다.,The Bank Clerk’s testimony will settle how the documents were handled. We must confirm the authenticity of the cancellation documents now.,銀行職員の証言で書類処理の過程を確定します。解約書類の真偽を今確認しなければなりません。,将通过银行职员的证言确认文件处理过程。现在必须确认解约文件真伪。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|hard].variants[judgewit-w-2-hard-v4].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|hard].variants[judgewit-w-2-hard-v4].text,은행 직원님을 부르겠습니다. 해지 절차의 빈틈이 이 사건의 핵심입니다.,I will call the Bank Clerk. The gap in the cancellation procedure is the core of this case.,銀行職員をお呼びします。解約手続きの隙が、この事件の核心です。,传唤银行职员。解约程序的漏洞是本案核心。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|hard].variants[judgewit-w-2-hard-v5].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|hard].variants[judgewit-w-2-hard-v5].text,은행 직원님께 바로 묻겠습니다. 이준호 씨 동의가 실제로 확인됐는지 명확히 들어야 합니다.,I will ask the Bank Clerk directly. We need to hear clearly whether Mr. Lee Jun-ho’s consent was actually confirmed.,銀行職員に直接尋ねます。イ・ジュノさんの同意が実際に確認されたのか、明確に聞く必要があります。,直接询问银行职员。必须明确听到是否实际确认了李俊浩先生的同意。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|mid].variants[judgewit-w-2-mid-v1].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|mid].variants[judgewit-w-2-mid-v1].text,은행 직원님 증언이 필요합니다. 해지 서류 절차가 쟁점이 된 만큼 접수와 확인 과정을 직접 듣겠습니다.,"We need testimony from the Bank Clerk. Since the cancellation document procedure is now at issue, I will hear directly about intake and verification.",銀行職員の証言が必要です。解約書類の手続きが争点になった以上、受付と確認の過程を直接聞きます。,需要银行职员的证言。既然解约文件程序已成争议点，我将直接听取接收和核验过程。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|mid].variants[judgewit-w-2-mid-v2].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|mid].variants[judgewit-w-2-mid-v2].text,"은행 직원님을 모시겠습니다. 공동 적금 해지가 정상 절차였는지, 서류에 어떤 의심점이 있었는지 확인하겠습니다.",I will call the Bank Clerk. We will confirm whether the joint savings account was cancelled through proper procedure and what raised doubts in the documents.,銀行職員をお呼びします。共同積立預金の解約が通常の手続きだったのか、書類にどのような疑問点があったのかを確認します。,传唤银行职员。确认共同储蓄账户解约是否走了正常程序，以及文件中有哪些疑点。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|mid].variants[judgewit-w-2-mid-v3].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|mid].variants[judgewit-w-2-mid-v3].text,해지 서류가 어떻게 처리됐는지 더 미룰 수 없습니다. 은행 직원님께 명의자 확인 과정을 묻겠습니다.,We can no longer put off how the cancellation documents were processed. I will ask the Bank Clerk about the account holder verification process.,解約書類がどう処理されたのか、これ以上先送りできません。銀行職員に名義人確認の過程を尋ねます。,不能再推迟确认解约文件是如何处理的。我将询问银行职员名义人核验过程。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|mid].variants[judgewit-w-2-mid-v4].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|mid].variants[judgewit-w-2-mid-v4].text,"은행 직원님, 해지 서류 접수 당시의 확인 절차와 미흡했던 부분을 구분해 말씀해 주십시오.","Bank Clerk, please distinguish the verification procedure at the time the cancellation documents were accepted from the parts that were lacking.",銀行職員、解約書類を受け付けた当時の確認手続きと、不十分だった部分を分けて述べてください。,银行职员，请区分说明接收解约文件当时的核验程序和不足之处。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|mid].variants[judgewit-w-2-mid-v5].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|mid].variants[judgewit-w-2-mid-v5].text,은행 직원님 증언으로 적금 해지의 권한 문제를 좁히겠습니다. 기록과 기억을 함께 듣겠습니다.,The Bank Clerk’s testimony will narrow the issue of authority over the savings cancellation. We will hear both the records and the clerk’s memory.,銀行職員の証言で、積立預金の解約権限の問題を絞ります。記録と記憶の両方を聞きます。,通过银行职员的证言缩小储蓄账户解约权限问题。记录和记忆都要听取。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|soft].variants[judgewit-w-2-soft-v1].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|soft].variants[judgewit-w-2-soft-v1].text,은행 직원님을 모시겠습니다. 공동 적금 해지 절차와 해지 서류 접수 과정을 차분히 확인하겠습니다.,I will call the Bank Clerk. We will calmly confirm the joint savings cancellation procedure and how the documents were accepted.,銀行職員をお呼びします。共同積立預金の解約手続きと解約書類の受付過程を落ち着いて確認します。,传唤银行职员。冷静确认共同储蓄账户解约程序和解约文件接收过程。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|soft].variants[judgewit-w-2-soft-v2].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|soft].variants[judgewit-w-2-soft-v2].text,은행 직원님께 먼저 묻겠습니다. 명의자 확인이 어떻게 이뤄졌고 어떤 서류가 들어왔는지 듣겠습니다.,I will first ask the Bank Clerk. We will hear how account holder verification was handled and what documents were submitted.,まず銀行職員に尋ねます。名義人確認がどのように行われ、どの書類が提出されたのかを聞きます。,先询问银行职员。听取名义人核验如何进行，以及提交了哪些文件。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|soft].variants[judgewit-w-2-soft-v3].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|soft].variants[judgewit-w-2-soft-v3].text,은행 직원님을 부르겠습니다. 해지 서류가 처리된 흐름을 기록 중심으로 확인하겠습니다.,"I will call the Bank Clerk. We will review the flow of how the cancellation documents were processed, centered on the records.",銀行職員をお呼びします。解約書類が処理された流れを、記録を中心に確認します。,传唤银行职员。以记录为中心确认解约文件的处理流程。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|soft].variants[judgewit-w-2-soft-v4].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|soft].variants[judgewit-w-2-soft-v4].text,"은행 직원님, 들어와 주십시오. 해지 서류와 적금 해지 절차를 순서대로 말씀해 주셔야 합니다.","Bank Clerk, please come in. You must state, in order, the cancellation documents and the savings cancellation procedure.",銀行職員、入ってください。解約書類と積立預金の解約手続きを順に述べていただきます。,银行职员，请进。请按顺序说明解约文件和储蓄账户解约程序。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|soft].variants[judgewit-w-2-soft-v5].behaviorHint,은행 직원 증언이 위임장 적금 해지 절차와 확인 미흡 가능성에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how the Bank Clerk’s testimony will bear on the power-of-attorney savings cancellation procedure and possible verification gaps.,銀行職員の証言が、委任状による積立預金の解約手続きと確認不足の可能性にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明银行职员的证言将如何影响委托书办理储蓄账户解约的程序及可能的核验不足。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-2|soft].variants[judgewit-w-2-soft-v5].text,은행 직원님의 업무상 기억을 통해 서류가 어디서 이상했는지부터 살펴보겠습니다.,"We will begin by examining, through the Bank Clerk’s professional memory, where the documents seemed irregular.",銀行職員の業務上の記憶を通じて、書類のどこに違和感があったのかから見ていきます。,通过银行职员的业务记忆，先查看文件从哪里开始显得异常。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|hard].variants[judgewit-w-3-hard-v1].behaviorHint,박미라 증언이 투자방 링크 전달과 박지연의 선제 송금 발언에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how Park Mi-ra’s testimony will bear on the investment chat link and Park Ji-yeon’s prior statement about transferring money.,パク・ミラの証言が、投資チャットのリンク共有とパク・ジヨンの先行送金発言にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明朴美罗的证言将如何影响投资群链接传递和朴智妍先行转账发言。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|hard].variants[judgewit-w-3-hard-v1].text,"박미라 씨, 들어오십시오. 투자방 링크 전달과 송금 경위에 관한 증언이 필요합니다.","Ms. Park Mi-ra, please come in. Testimony is needed on the investment chat link and the circumstances of the transfer.",パク・ミラさん、入ってください。投資チャットのリンク共有と送金の経緯について証言が必要です。,朴美罗女士，请进。需要你就投资群链接传递和转账经过作证。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|hard].variants[judgewit-w-3-hard-v2].behaviorHint,박미라 증언이 투자방 링크 전달과 박지연의 선제 송금 발언에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how Park Mi-ra’s testimony will bear on the investment chat link and Park Ji-yeon’s prior statement about transferring money.,パク・ミラの証言が、投資チャットのリンク共有とパク・ジヨンの先行送金発言にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明朴美罗的证言将如何影响投资群链接传递和朴智妍先行转账发言。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|hard].variants[judgewit-w-3-hard-v2].text,박미라 씨를 즉시 모시겠습니다. 박지연 씨의 돈 지키기 발언과 투자방 송금의 연결을 바로 확인하겠습니다.,I will call Ms. Park Mi-ra at once. We will immediately confirm the link between Ms. Park Ji-yeon’s statement about protecting her money and the transfer to the investment chat.,パク・ミラさんを直ちにお呼びします。パク・ジヨンさんの「お金を守る」という発言と投資チャットへの送金のつながりをすぐ確認します。,立即传唤朴美罗女士。马上确认朴智妍女士“守住钱”的发言与投资群转账之间的关联。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|hard].variants[judgewit-w-3-hard-v3].behaviorHint,박미라 증언이 투자방 링크 전달과 박지연의 선제 송금 발언에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how Park Mi-ra’s testimony will bear on the investment chat link and Park Ji-yeon’s prior statement about transferring money.,パク・ミラの証言が、投資チャットのリンク共有とパク・ジヨンの先行送金発言にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明朴美罗的证言将如何影响投资群链接传递和朴智妍先行转账发言。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|hard].variants[judgewit-w-3-hard-v3].text,박미라 씨 증언으로 투자방 손실의 시작을 확정하겠습니다. 더는 링크 전달 경위를 흐릴 수 없습니다.,Ms. Park Mi-ra’s testimony will settle the start of the investment chat loss. The circumstances of how the link was sent can no longer be blurred.,パク・ミラさんの証言で、投資チャットの損失の始まりを確定します。リンク共有の経緯をこれ以上曖昧にすることはできません。,将通过朴美罗女士的证言确认投资群损失的起点。不能再模糊链接传递经过。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|hard].variants[judgewit-w-3-hard-v4].behaviorHint,박미라 증언이 투자방 링크 전달과 박지연의 선제 송금 발언에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how Park Mi-ra’s testimony will bear on the investment chat link and Park Ji-yeon’s prior statement about transferring money.,パク・ミラの証言が、投資チャットのリンク共有とパク・ジヨンの先行送金発言にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明朴美罗的证言将如何影响投资群链接传递和朴智妍先行转账发言。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|hard].variants[judgewit-w-3-hard-v4].text,"박미라 씨, 링크를 보낸 시점과 박지연 씨가 먼저 한 말을 지금 명확히 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Park Mi-ra, please state clearly now when you sent the link and what Ms. Park Ji-yeon said first.",パク・ミラさん、リンクを送った時点と、パク・ジヨンさんが先に言ったことを今はっきり述べてください。,朴美罗女士，请现在明确说明你发送链接的时间点，以及朴智妍女士先说了什么。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|hard].variants[judgewit-w-3-hard-v5].behaviorHint,박미라 증언이 투자방 링크 전달과 박지연의 선제 송금 발언에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how Park Mi-ra’s testimony will bear on the investment chat link and Park Ji-yeon’s prior statement about transferring money.,パク・ミラの証言が、投資チャットのリンク共有とパク・ジヨンの先行送金発言にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明朴美罗的证言将如何影响投资群链接传递和朴智妍先行转账发言。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|hard].variants[judgewit-w-3-hard-v5].text,박미라 씨를 부르겠습니다. 이 사건의 돈 흐름을 판단하려면 투자방으로 들어간 길을 바로 들어야 합니다.,"I will call Ms. Park Mi-ra. To judge the money flow in this case, we need to hear directly how it entered the investment chat.",パク・ミラさんをお呼びします。この事件の金の流れを判断するには、投資チャットへ入った経路を直接聞く必要があります。,传唤朴美罗女士。要判断本案资金流向，就必须直接听取资金如何进入投资群。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|mid].variants[judgewit-w-3-mid-v1].behaviorHint,박미라 증언이 투자방 링크 전달과 박지연의 선제 송금 발언에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how Park Mi-ra’s testimony will bear on the investment chat link and Park Ji-yeon’s prior statement about transferring money.,パク・ミラの証言が、投資チャットのリンク共有とパク・ジヨンの先行送金発言にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明朴美罗的证言将如何影响投资群链接传递和朴智妍先行转账发言。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|mid].variants[judgewit-w-3-mid-v1].text,박미라 씨 증언이 필요합니다. 투자방 링크와 송금 결심의 순서를 직접 확인하겠습니다.,We need testimony from Ms. Park Mi-ra. I will confirm directly the order between the investment chat link and the decision to transfer money.,パク・ミラさんの証言が必要です。投資チャットのリンクと送金を決めた順序を直接確認します。,需要朴美罗女士的证言。我将直接确认投资群链接与转账决定的先后顺序。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|mid].variants[judgewit-w-3-mid-v2].behaviorHint,박미라 증언이 투자방 링크 전달과 박지연의 선제 송금 발언에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how Park Mi-ra’s testimony will bear on the investment chat link and Park Ji-yeon’s prior statement about transferring money.,パク・ミラの証言が、投資チャットのリンク共有とパク・ジヨンの先行送金発言にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明朴美罗的证言将如何影响投资群链接传递和朴智妍先行转账发言。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|mid].variants[judgewit-w-3-mid-v2].text,박미라 씨를 모시겠습니다. 박지연 씨가 돈부터 지키겠다고 말한 시점과 링크 전달 시점을 구분해야 합니다.,I will call Ms. Park Mi-ra. We must distinguish when Ms. Park Ji-yeon said she would protect her money first from when the link was sent.,パク・ミラさんをお呼びします。パク・ジヨンさんが「お金を先に守る」と言った時点と、リンク共有の時点を区別しなければなりません。,传唤朴美罗女士。必须区分朴智妍女士说要先守住钱的时间点与链接传递时间点。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|mid].variants[judgewit-w-3-mid-v3].behaviorHint,박미라 증언이 투자방 링크 전달과 박지연의 선제 송금 발언에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how Park Mi-ra’s testimony will bear on the investment chat link and Park Ji-yeon’s prior statement about transferring money.,パク・ミラの証言が、投資チャットのリンク共有とパク・ジヨンの先行送金発言にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明朴美罗的证言将如何影响投资群链接传递和朴智妍先行转账发言。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|mid].variants[judgewit-w-3-mid-v3].text,투자방으로 돈이 움직인 경위를 더 미룰 수 없습니다. 박미라 씨에게 대화 순서를 묻겠습니다.,We can no longer put off how the money moved into the investment chat. I will ask Ms. Park Mi-ra about the order of the conversation.,投資チャットへ金が動いた経緯を、これ以上先送りできません。パク・ミラさんに会話の順序を尋ねます。,不能再推迟确认资金进入投资群的经过。我要询问朴美罗女士对话顺序。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|mid].variants[judgewit-w-3-mid-v4].behaviorHint,박미라 증언이 투자방 링크 전달과 박지연의 선제 송금 발언에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how Park Mi-ra’s testimony will bear on the investment chat link and Park Ji-yeon’s prior statement about transferring money.,パク・ミラの証言が、投資チャットのリンク共有とパク・ジヨンの先行送金発言にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明朴美罗的证言将如何影响投资群链接传递和朴智妍先行转账发言。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|mid].variants[judgewit-w-3-mid-v4].text,"박미라 씨, 링크를 보낸 사실과 박지연 씨의 발언을 각각 분리해 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Park Mi-ra, please separate the fact that you sent the link from Ms. Park Ji-yeon’s statement.",パク・ミラさん、リンクを送った事実とパク・ジヨンさんの発言を、それぞれ分けて述べてください。,朴美罗女士，请把你发送链接的事实和朴智妍女士的发言分别说明。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|mid].variants[judgewit-w-3-mid-v5].behaviorHint,박미라 증언이 투자방 링크 전달과 박지연의 선제 송금 발언에 미치는 영향을 재판관이 먼저 밝힌다.,The Judge first states how Park Mi-ra’s testimony will bear on the investment chat link and Park Ji-yeon’s prior statement about transferring money.,パク・ミラの証言が、投資チャットのリンク共有とパク・ジヨンの先行送金発言にどう関わるかを裁判官が先に示す。,法官先说明朴美罗的证言将如何影响投资群链接传递和朴智妍先行转账发言。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
,non_party_scripted_text,src/data/scriptedText,spouse-01,channels[judge_witness_summon].entries[w-3|mid].variants[judgewit-w-3-mid-v5].text,박미라 씨 증언으로 투자 손실 경위와 박지연 씨의 선제 행동을 좁히겠습니다.,Ms. Park Mi-ra’s testimony will narrow the circumstances of the investment loss and Ms. Park Ji-yeon’s prior action.,パク・ミラさんの証言で、投資損失の経緯とパク・ジヨンさんの先行行動を絞ります。,通过朴美罗女士的证言，缩小投资损失经过和朴智妍女士先行行动的范围。,"Scripted text channel without party a/b as speaker: system, judge, witness, dossier, mediation, aftermath, and milestone copy."
