,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-3].variants[judgeq-d-3-motive_search-b-pattern_warning-v4].behaviorHint,동기 탐색. 닮음을 끝까지 정리해 말하지 못한 본인의 망설임을 답하게 한다. 차용금 미상환 단정은 보류한다.,Motive search. Focus on why you treated the pattern as something that required warning. Ask why the choice was made while separating motive from proven facts.,動機確認。そのパターンを警告すべきものと見た理由に焦点を当てる。動機と確認済み事実を分けて、選択の理由を尋ねる。,动机确认。聚焦你为何把这个模式视为必须提醒的事。把动机与已确认事实分开，追问其选择理由。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-3].variants[judgeq-d-3-motive_search-b-pattern_warning-v4].text,본인이 가진 비교 근거를 다 펼쳐 놓지 못한 자리에 어떤 부담이 있었는지 답하십시오.,"Ms. Choi Su-min, if your judgment narrowed at that moment, explain what made it narrow without adding a conclusion.",チェ・スミンさん、その時点で判断が狭まったなら、結論を加えず何がそうさせたのか説明してください。,崔秀敏女士，如果当时你的判断开始收窄，请不要加入结论，只说明是什么让它收窄。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-3].variants[judgeq-d-3-motive_search-b-pattern_warning-v5].behaviorHint,동기 탐색. 닮음을 끝까지 정리해 말하지 못한 본인의 망설임을 답하게 한다. 차용금 미상환 단정은 보류한다.,Motive search. Focus on why you treated the pattern as something that required warning. Ask why the choice was made while separating motive from proven facts.,動機確認。そのパターンを警告すべきものと見た理由に焦点を当てる。動機と確認済み事実を分けて、選択の理由を尋ねる。,动机确认。聚焦你为何把这个模式视为必须提醒的事。把动机与已确认事实分开，追问其选择理由。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-3].variants[judgeq-d-3-motive_search-b-pattern_warning-v5].text,"최수민 씨, 그 비교를 끝내 보류한 결과로 본인이 떠안은 손해를 본인 쪽에서 어떻게 정리하는지 답해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi Su-min, tell the court what you were trying to protect or avoid when dealing with why you treated the pattern as something that required warning.",チェ・スミンさん、そのパターンを警告すべきものと見た理由に向き合う中で、何を守り、何を避けようとしていたのか述べてください。,崔秀敏女士，处理你为何把这个模式视为必须提醒的事时，你想保护什么，又想避开什么？,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v1_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v1].behaviorHint,사정 확인. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Circumstance check. Have the answer address the weight of the IOU.,事情確認。借用書の重さという角度から答えさせる。,情况确认。让回答围绕借条的分量展开。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v1_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v1].text,"송다은 씨, 아버지의 차용증을 확인했을 때 먼저 든 감정에 대해 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, please describe the first feeling you had when you confirmed your father's IOU.",ソン・ダウンさん、父の借用書を確認したとき、最初に浮かんだ感情を話してください。,宋多恩女士，请说明您确认父亲的借条时，最先涌上的是什么感受。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v2_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v2].behaviorHint,사정 확인. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Circumstance check. Have the answer address the weight of the IOU.,事情確認。借用書の重さという角度から答えさせる。,情况确认。让回答围绕借条的分量展开。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v2_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v2].text,"송다은 씨, 차용증의 무게을 지금 다시 보면 어떤 감정이 앞서는지 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, looking back now at the weight of the IOU, what feeling comes first?",ソン・ダウンさん、借用書の重さを今あらためて見ると、どの感情が先に立ちますか。,宋多恩女士，现在重新面对这份借条的分量，最先出现的是什么情绪？,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v3_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v3].behaviorHint,사정 확인. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Circumstance check. Have the answer address the weight of the IOU.,事情確認。借用書の重さという角度から答えさせる。,情况确认。让回答围绕借条的分量展开。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v3_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v3].text,"송다은 씨, 그때 말하지 못했거나 보지 못했던 부분을 솔직히 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, please explain honestly what you could not say or could not see at the time.",ソン・ダウンさん、当時言えなかったこと、見えていなかったことを率直に説明してください。,宋多恩女士，请坦率说明当时没能说出口或没能看见的部分。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v4_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v4].behaviorHint,사정 확인. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Circumstance check. Have the answer address the weight of the IOU.,事情確認。借用書の重さという角度から答えさせる。,情况确认。让回答围绕借条的分量展开。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v4_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v4].text,"송다은 씨, 당시 감정과 지금의 판단을 나눠 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, please separate what you felt then from how you judge it now.",ソン・ダウンさん、当時の感情と今の判断を分けて話してください。,宋多恩女士，请把当时的情绪和现在的判断分开说明。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v5_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v5].behaviorHint,사정 확인. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Circumstance check. Have the answer address the weight of the IOU.,事情確認。借用書の重さという角度から答えさせる。,情况确认。让回答围绕借条的分量展开。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v5_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-loan_document_weight-v5].text,"송다은 씨, 이 쟁점이 본인에게 가장 부담스러운 이유를 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, please explain why this issue weighs most heavily on you.",ソン・ダウンさん、この争点がご自身にとって最も重い理由を話してください。,宋多恩女士，请说明这个争点为什么对您来说最沉重。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v1_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v1].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 침묵을 손절로 굳힌 송다은의 해석을 인정하고 다른 가능성 검토 여부를 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v1_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v1].text,"송다은 씨, 친구의 침묵이 본인에게는 손절의 증거로 보였을 겁니다. 그 감정을 인정하면서, 그 침묵을 다른 가능성으로 한 번이라도 의심해 본 적이 있었는지 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, please describe what feeling comes first when you face the silence meant to protect someone.",ソン・ダウンさん、守るための沈黙に向き合うとき最初に浮かぶ感情を話してください。,宋多恩女士，面对出于保护的沉默时，请说明最先出现的感受。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v2_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v2].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 보호 침묵 가설에 대한 송다은의 현재 수용 범위를 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v2_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v2].text,"친구가 본인을 보호하려 침묵했을 가능성을 지금에 와서 어디까지 받아들일 수 있는지, 솔직히 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, looking at the silence meant to protect someone again now, what feeling comes first?",ソン・ダウンさん、今あらためて守るための沈黙を見ると、どの感情が先に立ちますか。,宋多恩女士，现在重新看出于保护的沉默，最先浮现的是什么情绪？,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v3_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v3].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 결혼 직전 본인이 침묵 이유 추궁을 미룬 결을 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v3_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v3].text,"본인이 침묵의 이유를 묻기 어려웠던 결혼 직전의 시기가 있었다면, 그 어려움을 그대로 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, explain honestly what you could not say or could not see at that time.",ソン・ダウンさん、当時言えなかったこと、見えていなかったことを率直に説明してください。,宋多恩女士，请坦率说明当时没能说出口或没能看见的部分。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v4_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v4].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 침묵에 본인이 붙여 온 단어를 본인이 다시 보게 한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v4_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v4].text,"친구의 침묵을 본인이 어떤 단어로 정리해 왔는지, 그 단어가 정확했는지 다시 보아 주십시오.","Ms. Song, separate what you felt then from how you judge it now.",ソン・ダウンさん、当時の感情と今の判断を分けて話してください。,宋多恩女士，请把当时的情绪和现在的判断分开说明。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v5_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v5].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 침묵 앞 본인의 가장 가혹한 짐작을 본인이 직접 짚게 한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v5_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-protective_silence-v5].text,"송다은 씨, 본인이 그 침묵 앞에서 했던 가장 가혹한 짐작이 무엇이었는지, 단정 없이 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, please tell the court why this issue weighs so heavily on you.",ソン・ダウンさん、この争点がご自身に重くのしかかる理由を話してください。,宋多恩女士，请说明这个争点为什么对您如此沉重。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v1_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v1].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 손절로 굳어진 본인의 해석을 인정하고 빈칸 메움의 결을 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the gap in the messages before the old fallout. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从旧日决裂前聊天中的空白的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v1_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v1].text,"송다은 씨, 친구의 마지막 메시지가 ""내가 정리하겠다""였고 그 뒤로 연락이 끊긴 일은 본인에게는 그 자체가 손절의 이유처럼 굳어졌을 겁니다. 그 감정을 인정하면서, 본인이 그 빈칸을 어떤 짐작으로 메워 왔는지 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, please describe what feeling comes first when you face the gap in the messages before the old fallout.",ソン・ダウンさん、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白に向き合うとき最初に浮かぶ感情を話してください。,宋多恩女士，面对旧日决裂前聊天中的空白时，请说明最先出现的感受。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v2_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v2].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 미확인 멈춤 이후 결론이 굳은 흐름을 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the gap in the messages before the old fallout. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从旧日决裂前聊天中的空白的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v2_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v2].text,"그때 본인이 친구의 사정을 끝까지 묻지 않고 멈췄다면, 그 멈춤이 본인 안에서 어떤 결론으로 굳어졌는지 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, looking at the gap in the messages before the old fallout again now, what feeling comes first?",ソン・ダウンさん、今あらためて過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白を見ると、どの感情が先に立ちますか。,宋多恩女士，现在重新看旧日决裂前聊天中的空白，最先浮现的是什么情绪？,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v3_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v3].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 첫 연상 인물을 끌어내고 차용금 미상환 단정은 보류한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the gap in the messages before the old fallout. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从旧日决裂前聊天中的空白的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v3_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v3].text,"""정리하겠다""는 한마디 뒤에 본인이 가장 먼저 떠올린 사람이 누구였는지, 단정 없이 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, explain honestly what you could not say or could not see at that time.",ソン・ダウンさん、当時言えなかったこと、見えていなかったことを率直に説明してください。,宋多恩女士，请坦率说明当时没能说出口或没能看见的部分。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v4_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v4].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 본인의 짐작이 단일이었는지 다중이었는지 그 변화를 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the gap in the messages before the old fallout. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从旧日决裂前聊天中的空白的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v4_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v4].text,"친구가 무엇을 정리하려 했는지에 대한 본인의 짐작이 한 가지였는지 여러 가지였는지, 그 변화를 솔직히 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, separate what you felt then from how you judge it now.",ソン・ダウンさん、当時の感情と今の判断を分けて話してください。,宋多恩女士，请把当时的情绪和现在的判断分开说明。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v5_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v5].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 끝까지 묻지 않은 결정의 이유를 본인 시점에서 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the gap in the messages before the old fallout. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从旧日决裂前聊天中的空白的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v5_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-severance_chat_gap-v5].text,"송다은 씨, 본인이 그 빈칸을 끝내 묻지 않기로 한 결정이 있다면, 그 결정의 이유를 결론 없이 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, please tell the court why this issue weighs so heavily on you.",ソン・ダウンさん、この争点がご自身に重くのしかかる理由を話してください。,宋多恩女士，请说明这个争点为什么对您如此沉重。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v1_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v1].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 가족 관련 수치를 인정하고 직접 인지/간접 인지를 분리하게 한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the transfer and repayment records. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、送金と返済記録の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从转账与还款记录的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v1_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v1].text,"송다은 씨, 본인 가족과 관련된 돈 거래가 법정에서 거론되는 일은 큰 수치일 수 있습니다. 그 감정을 인정하면서, 본인이 직접 알고 있는 송금 정황과 들어서 알게 된 부분을 그대로 구분해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, please describe what feeling comes first when you face the transfer and repayment records.",ソン・ダウンさん、送金と返済記録に向き合うとき最初に浮かぶ感情を話してください。,宋多恩女士，面对转账与还款记录时，请说明最先出现的感受。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v2_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v2].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 본인 사각의 가능성을 어디까지 열어 두는지 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the transfer and repayment records. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、送金と返済記録の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从转账与还款记录的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v2_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v2].text,"본인이 모르고 지나간 돈 흐름이 있을 가능성을 어디까지 열어 두고 있는지, 솔직히 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, looking at the transfer and repayment records again now, what feeling comes first?",ソン・ダウンさん、今あらためて送金と返済記録を見ると、どの感情が先に立ちますか。,宋多恩女士，现在重新看转账与还款记录，最先浮现的是什么情绪？,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v3_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v3].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 동일 사건 여부 자체의 헷갈림을 인정하게 한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the transfer and repayment records. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、送金と返済記録の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从转账与还款记录的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v3_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v3].text,"친구가 말하는 송금이 본인이 기억하는 사건과 같은 일인지 다른 일인지조차 헷갈린다면, 그 헷갈림 자체를 그대로 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, explain honestly what you could not say or could not see at that time.",ソン・ダウンさん、当時言えなかったこと、見えていなかったことを率直に説明してください。,宋多恩女士，请坦率说明当时没能说出口或没能看见的部分。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v4_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v4].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 상환 미확인 표현에 대한 본인의 수용 마음을 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the transfer and repayment records. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、送金と返済記録の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从转账与还款记录的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v4_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v4].text,"""상환이 확인되지 않는다""는 표현을 본인이 어떻게 받아들이고 있는지, 결론을 미루고 그 마음만 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, separate what you felt then from how you judge it now.",ソン・ダウンさん、当時の感情と今の判断を分けて話してください。,宋多恩女士，请把当时的情绪和现在的判断分开说明。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v5_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v5].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 가족 금전 문제 직접 확인 회피의 결을 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the transfer and repayment records. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。ソン・ダウンさんに、送金と返済記録の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导宋多恩女士从转账与还款记录的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v5_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-a-transfer_repayment-v5].text,"송다은 씨, 본인이 가족의 돈 문제를 끝까지 직접 묻지 못한 이유가 있다면, 그 이유의 결을 단정 없이 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, please tell the court why this issue weighs so heavily on you.",ソン・ダウンさん、この争点がご自身に重くのしかかる理由を話してください。,宋多恩女士，请说明这个争点为什么对您如此沉重。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v1_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v1].behaviorHint,사정 확인. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Circumstance check. Have the answer address the weight of the IOU.,事情確認。借用書の重さという角度から答えさせる。,情况确认。让回答围绕借条的分量展开。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v1_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v1].text,"최수민 씨, 친구 아버지의 돈 문제를 말해야 하는 부담에 대해 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, please describe what feeling comes first when you face the weight of the IOU.",チェ・スミンさん、借用書の重さに向き合うとき最初に浮かぶ感情を話してください。,崔秀敏女士，面对借条的分量时，请说明最先出现的感受。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v2_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v2].behaviorHint,사정 확인. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Circumstance check. Have the answer address the weight of the IOU.,事情確認。借用書の重さという角度から答えさせる。,情况确认。让回答围绕借条的分量展开。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v2_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v2].text,"최수민 씨, 차용증의 무게을 지금 다시 보면 어떤 감정이 앞서는지 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, looking at the weight of the IOU again now, what feeling comes first?",チェ・スミンさん、今あらためて借用書の重さを見ると、どの感情が先に立ちますか。,崔秀敏女士，现在重新看借条的分量，最先浮现的是什么情绪？,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v3_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v3].behaviorHint,사정 확인. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Circumstance check. Have the answer address the weight of the IOU.,事情確認。借用書の重さという角度から答えさせる。,情况确认。让回答围绕借条的分量展开。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v3_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v3].text,"최수민 씨, 그때 말하지 못했거나 보지 못했던 부분을 솔직히 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, explain honestly what you could not say or could not see at that time.",チェ・スミンさん、当時言えなかったこと、見えていなかったことを率直に説明してください。,崔秀敏女士，请坦率说明当时没能说出口或没能看见的部分。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v4_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v4].behaviorHint,사정 확인. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Circumstance check. Have the answer address the weight of the IOU.,事情確認。借用書の重さという角度から答えさせる。,情况确认。让回答围绕借条的分量展开。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v4_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v4].text,"최수민 씨, 당시 감정과 지금의 판단을 나눠 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, separate what you felt then from how you judge it now.",チェ・スミンさん、当時の感情と今の判断を分けて話してください。,崔秀敏女士，请把当时的情绪和现在的判断分开说明。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v5_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v5].behaviorHint,사정 확인. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Circumstance check. Have the answer address the weight of the IOU.,事情確認。借用書の重さという角度から答えさせる。,情况确认。让回答围绕借条的分量展开。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v5_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-loan_document_weight-v5].text,"최수민 씨, 이 쟁점이 본인에게 가장 부담스러운 이유를 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, please tell the court why this issue weighs so heavily on you.",チェ・スミンさん、この争点がご自身に重くのしかかる理由を話してください。,崔秀敏女士，请说明这个争点为什么对您如此沉重。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v1_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v1].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 보호 악역의 침묵을 정면 인정하되 차용금 미상환 확정은 보류한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v1_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v1].text,"최수민 씨, 친구를 다치지 않게 하려고 본인이 악역을 자처한 시간은 누구에게도 쉽게 설명되지 않았을 겁니다. 그 침묵의 무게를 결론까지 풀지 말고 어떤 결이었는지만 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, please describe what feeling comes first when you face the silence meant to protect someone.",チェ・スミンさん、守るための沈黙に向き合うとき最初に浮かぶ感情を話してください。,崔秀敏女士，面对出于保护的沉默时，请说明最先出现的感受。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v2_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v2].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 가장 견디기 힘든 침묵 장면 한 컷만 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v2_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v2].text,"본인이 견딘 침묵 가운데 가장 견디기 힘들었던 한 장면을, 단정 없이 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, looking at the silence meant to protect someone again now, what feeling comes first?",チェ・スミンさん、今あらためて守るための沈黙を見ると、どの感情が先に立ちますか。,崔秀敏女士，现在重新看出于保护的沉默，最先浮现的是什么情绪？,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v3_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v3].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 본인 침묵의 부작용을 본인이 안고 있는 결을 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v3_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v3].text,"침묵을 택한 본인의 판단이 결과적으로 친구의 오해를 키웠다는 점을, 본인은 어떻게 안고 있는지 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, explain honestly what you could not say or could not see at that time.",チェ・スミンさん、当時言えなかったこと、見えていなかったことを率直に説明してください。,崔秀敏女士，请坦率说明当时没能说出口或没能看见的部分。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v4_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v4].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 다른 선택 가정을 결론 없이 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v4_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v4].text,"다른 선택지가 있었다면 본인이 무엇을 다르게 했을지, 그 가정도 결론 없이 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, separate what you felt then from how you judge it now.",チェ・スミンさん、当時の感情と今の判断を分けて話してください。,崔秀敏女士，请把当时的情绪和现在的判断分开说明。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v5_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v5].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 두 방향 침묵 동기의 비중을 본인이 직접 비교하게 한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v5_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-protective_silence-v5].text,"친구를 위한 침묵과 본인을 위한 침묵 가운데 어느 쪽이 더 컸는지, 솔직히 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, please tell the court why this issue weighs so heavily on you.",チェ・スミンさん、この争点がご自身に重くのしかかる理由を話してください。,崔秀敏女士，请说明这个争点为什么对您如此沉重。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v1_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v1].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 메시지 작성 시 본인의 발화 한계 결정을 끌어내고 차용금 미상환 직접 발설은 차단한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the gap in the messages before the old fallout. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从旧日决裂前聊天中的空白的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v1_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v1].text,"최수민 씨, ""내가 정리하겠다""라고 적은 뒤 친구에게 아무 설명도 남기지 못하고 멀어진 일이 본인에게도 무거웠을 겁니다. 그 메시지를 적는 순간 본인이 어디까지는 말할 수 있고 어디서는 멈춰야 한다고 결정했는지 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, please describe what feeling comes first when you face the gap in the messages before the old fallout.",チェ・スミンさん、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白に向き合うとき最初に浮かぶ感情を話してください。,崔秀敏女士，面对旧日决裂前聊天中的空白时，请说明最先出现的感受。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v2_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v2].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 보호 침묵의 부작용(악역화)을 본인이 안고 있는 결을 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the gap in the messages before the old fallout. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从旧日决裂前聊天中的空白的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v2_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v2].text,"친구를 다치지 않게 하려고 빈칸으로 두기로 한 부분이 결과적으로 본인을 악역으로 만들었다는 점을, 본인은 어떻게 안고 있는지 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, looking at the gap in the messages before the old fallout again now, what feeling comes first?",チェ・スミンさん、今あらためて過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白を見ると、どの感情が先に立ちますか。,崔秀敏女士，现在重新看旧日决裂前聊天中的空白，最先浮现的是什么情绪？,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v3_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v3].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 그 시기 본인의 짐 결만 끌어내고 S5 진실은 보호한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the gap in the messages before the old fallout. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从旧日决裂前聊天中的空白的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v3_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v3].text,그 시기에 본인이 짊어진 짐의 결만이라도 말씀해 주십시오. 결론까지 풀 필요는 없습니다.,"Ms. Choi, explain honestly what you could not say or could not see at that time.",チェ・スミンさん、当時言えなかったこと、見えていなかったことを率直に説明してください。,崔秀敏女士，请坦率说明当时没能说出口或没能看见的部分。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v4_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v4].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 침묵 동기의 두 방향(타자 보호/자기 보호) 중 어느 쪽이 컸는지 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the gap in the messages before the old fallout. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从旧日决裂前聊天中的空白的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v4_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v4].text,"""정리하겠다""는 말 뒤에 본인이 침묵을 택한 이유가 친구를 위한 것이었는지 본인을 위한 것이었는지, 솔직히 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, separate what you felt then from how you judge it now.",チェ・スミンさん、当時の感情と今の判断を分けて話してください。,崔秀敏女士，请把当时的情绪和现在的判断分开说明。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v5_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v5].behaviorHint,"공감 접근. ""손절"" 단어를 빼고 본인 시점의 그 시간을 풀게 한다.",Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the gap in the messages before the old fallout. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、過去の絶交前のメッセージの空白の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从旧日决裂前聊天中的空白的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v5_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-severance_chat_gap-v5].text,"손절로 보이는 그 시간이 본인에게는 어떤 시간이었는지, ""손절""이라는 단어 없이 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, please tell the court why this issue weighs so heavily on you.",チェ・スミンさん、この争点がご自身に重くのしかかる理由を話してください。,崔秀敏女士，请说明这个争点为什么对您如此沉重。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v1_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v1].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 송금 확인 흔적과 미확인 상환을 본인이 정리하게 하고 차용금 미상환 단정은 보류한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the transfer and repayment records. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、送金と返済記録の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从转账与还款记录的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v1_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v1].text,"최수민 씨, 친구의 가족과 얽힌 돈 문제를 본인 입으로 다시 꺼내야 하는 일이 가볍지 않을 겁니다. 본인이 직접 확인한 송금 흔적과 아직 확인되지 않은 상환 사이를, 결론 없이 정리해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, please describe what feeling comes first when you face the transfer and repayment records.",チェ・スミンさん、送金と返済記録に向き合うとき最初に浮かぶ感情を話してください。,崔秀敏女士，面对转账与还款记录时，请说明最先出现的感受。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v2_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v2].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 미상환 손해의 윤곽만 끌어내고 차용금 미상환 단정은 보류한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the transfer and repayment records. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、送金と返済記録の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从转账与还款记录的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v2_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v2].text,"본인이 그 돈을 끝내 다 돌려받지 못한 부분이 있다면, 그 손해의 윤곽만이라도 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, looking at the transfer and repayment records again now, what feeling comes first?",チェ・スミンさん、今あらためて送金と返済記録を見ると、どの感情が先に立ちますか。,崔秀敏女士，现在重新看转账与还款记录，最先浮现的是什么情绪？,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v3_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v3].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 기록 보관 동기를 본인이 직접 풀게 한다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the transfer and repayment records. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、送金と返済記録の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从转账与还款记录的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v3_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v3].text,"영수증과 계좌 흔적을 보관해 둔 이유가 단순 기록이었는지, 아니면 다른 마음이 있었는지 솔직히 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, explain honestly what you could not say or could not see at that time.",チェ・スミンさん、当時言えなかったこと、見えていなかったことを率直に説明してください。,崔秀敏女士，请坦率说明当时没能说出口或没能看见的部分。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v4_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v4].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 친구에게 침묵한 결정의 자기 부담을 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the transfer and repayment records. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、送金と返済記録の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从转账与还款记录的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v4_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v4].text,"송금 이야기를 친구에게 말하지 않은 본인의 결정이 본인을 더 무겁게 만든 부분이 있다면, 그 무게를 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, separate what you felt then from how you judge it now.",チェ・スミンさん、当時の感情と今の判断を分けて話してください。,崔秀敏女士，请把当时的情绪和现在的判断分开说明。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v5_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v5].behaviorHint,공감 접근. 상환 미확인 표현에 대한 본인의 수용 입장을 끌어낸다.,Empathy approach. Guide Ms. Choi to answer from the angle of the transfer and repayment records. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,共感的アプローチ。チェ・スミンさんに、送金と返済記録の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,共情式切入。引导崔秀敏女士从转账与还款记录的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v5_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-empathy_approach-b-transfer_repayment-v5].text,"""상환이 확인되지 않는다""는 표현을 본인이 받아들이는 방식을, 단정이 아니라 본인의 입장에서 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Choi, please tell the court why this issue weighs so heavily on you.",チェ・スミンさん、この争点がご自身に重くのしかかる理由を話してください。,崔秀敏女士，请说明这个争点为什么对您如此沉重。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v1_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v1].behaviorHint,사실 추궁. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Fact pursuit. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the weight of the IOU. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,事実追及。ソン・ダウンさんに、借用書の重さの角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,事实追问。引导宋多恩女士从借条的分量的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v1_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v1].text,"송다은 씨, 차용증과 일부 상환 내역을 처음 알게 된 시점과 직접 확인한 자료에 대해 기록 기준으로 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, state when you first learned of the weight of the IOU and what you confirmed directly, based on the record.",ソン・ダウンさん、借用書の重さを初めて知った時点と直接確認した資料を、記録に基づいて述べてください。,宋多恩女士，请依据记录说明您最初得知借条的分量的时间，以及直接确认过的资料。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v2_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v2].behaviorHint,사실 추궁. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Fact pursuit. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the weight of the IOU. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,事実追及。ソン・ダウンさんに、借用書の重さの角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,事实追问。引导宋多恩女士从借条的分量的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v2_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v2].text,"송다은 씨, 차용증의 무게에 관해 확인한 부분과 추정한 부분을 구분해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, separate what you personally verified about the weight of the IOU from what you inferred.",ソン・ダウンさん、借用書の重さについて本人が確認した部分と推測した部分を分けてください。,宋多恩女士，请区分您对借条的分量亲自确认的部分和推定的部分。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v3_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v3].behaviorHint,사실 추궁. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Fact pursuit. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the weight of the IOU. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,事実追及。ソン・ダウンさんに、借用書の重さの角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,事实追问。引导宋多恩女士从借条的分量的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v3_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v3].text,"송다은 씨, 차용증과 일부 상환 내역을 처음 알게 된 시점과 직접 확인한 자료이 이 쟁점에서 어떤 의미인지 설명해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, explain what the weight of the IOU means for this issue, using the record as your basis.",ソン・ダウンさん、この争点において借用書の重さが何を意味するのか、記録を基準に説明してください。,宋多恩女士，请以记录为准说明借条的分量在这个争点中意味着什么。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v4_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v4].behaviorHint,사실 추궁. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Fact pursuit. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the weight of the IOU. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,事実追及。ソン・ダウンさんに、借用書の重さの角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,事实追问。引导宋多恩女士从借条的分量的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v4_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v4].text,"송다은 씨, 차용증의 무게에서 본인이 직접 확인한 사실과 나중에 알게 된 사실을 나눠 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, distinguish the facts you directly confirmed from those you learned later.",ソン・ダウンさん、直接確認した事実と後から知った事実を分けて話してください。,宋多恩女士，请区分您直接确认的事实和后来得知的事实。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v5_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v5].behaviorHint,사실 추궁. 차용증의 무게 각도에서 답하게 한다.,Fact pursuit. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the weight of the IOU. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,事実追及。ソン・ダウンさんに、借用書の重さの角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,事实追问。引导宋多恩女士从借条的分量的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v5_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-loan_document_weight-v5].text,"송다은 씨, 이 부분이 기존 진술과 어떻게 이어지는지 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, explain how this point connects to your previous statement.",ソン・ダウンさん、この部分がこれまでの陳述とどうつながるのかを話してください。,宋多恩女士，请说明这一部分如何接续此前陈述。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v1_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v1].behaviorHint,사실 추궁. 손절 후 재확인 시도와 청취 경로를 사실관계로 답하게 한다.,Fact pursuit. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,事実追及。ソン・ダウンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,事实追问。引导宋多恩女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v1_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v1].text,"송다은 씨, 손절 이후 최수민 씨에게 그 이유를 다시 물어본 시점이 있다면 언제였는지 순서대로 말씀해 주십시오.","Ms. Song, state when you first learned of the silence meant to protect someone and what you confirmed directly, based on the record.",ソン・ダウンさん、守るための沈黙を初めて知った時点と直接確認した資料を、記録に基づいて述べてください。,宋多恩女士，请依据记录说明您最初得知出于保护的沉默的时间，以及直接确认过的资料。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v2_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v2].behaviorHint,사실 추궁. 손절 후 재확인 시도와 청취 경로를 사실관계로 답하게 한다.,Fact pursuit. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,事実追及。ソン・ダウンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,事实追问。引导宋多恩女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v2_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v2].text,그때 본인이 직접 들은 답과 다른 사람을 통해 추정한 답을 구분해 주십시오.,"Ms. Song, separate what you personally verified about the silence meant to protect someone from what you inferred.",ソン・ダウンさん、守るための沈黙について本人が確認した部分と推測した部分を分けてください。,宋多恩女士，请区分您对出于保护的沉默亲自确认的部分和推定的部分。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v3_.behaviorHint,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v3].behaviorHint,사실 추궁. 손절 후 재확인 시도와 청취 경로를 사실관계로 답하게 한다.,Fact pursuit. Guide Ms. Song to answer from the angle of the silence meant to protect someone. Keep the tone controlled and do not force a premature conclusion.,事実追及。ソン・ダウンさんに、守るための沈黙の角度から答えさせる。口調は抑え、早すぎる結論を強要しない。,事实追问。引导宋多恩女士从出于保护的沉默的角度作答。保持语气克制，不强行导向过早结论。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
judge_question_script_src_data_scriptedAngles_friend-01_judgeQuestions_d-4_.variants_judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v3_.text,judge_question_script,src/data/scriptedAngles,friend-01,judgeQuestions[d-4].variants[judgeq-d-4-fact_pursuit-a-protective_silence-v3].text,"""수민이가 변심했다""는 본인의 정리와 그 시기 카톡에 적힌 마지막 단어가 어긋나는 부분이 있다면 짚어 주십시오.","Ms. Song, explain what the silence meant to protect someone means for this issue, using the record as your basis.",ソン・ダウンさん、この争点において守るための沈黙が何を意味するのか、記録を基準に説明してください。,宋多恩女士，请以记录为准说明出于保护的沉默在这个争点中意味着什么。,Judge-authored interrogation question or judge behavior hint.
